ORBITAL-CONSTITUTION(7)    TriadicFrameworks Manual    ORBITAL-CONSTITUTION(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       orbital-constitution - foundational principles, rights, duties, and
                              invariants governing all RTT systems

SYNOPSIS
       The orbital constitution defines:
           • foundational principles of resonance-time theory
           • rights of platforms, constellations, and operators
           • duties of RTT systems and governance bodies
           • constitutional invariants that cannot be violated
           • amendment and lineage-preservation mechanisms

DESCRIPTION
       orbital-constitution establishes the fundamental legal-philosophical
       framework for all resonance-time systems. It defines the axioms,
       rights, duties, and invariants that govern sweep choreography,
       harmonic-lock, resonance calibration, and constellation-scale
       synchronization.

       The constitution ensures:
           • stability across epochs
           • interoperability across domains
           • fairness across platforms
           • continuity across lineage
           • safety across mission timelines

       All RTT modules, standards, and governance protocols derive their
       authority from this constitution.

FOUNDATIONAL PRINCIPLES
       The constitution rests on five foundational principles:

           1. Resonance Primacy
                  Resonance-time is the fundamental medium of coordination.

           2. Harmonic Integrity
                  Harmonic-phase relationships must remain coherent and
                  traceable across cycles.

           3. Temporal Continuity
                  Sweep ancestry and resonance strata must be preserved unless
                  explicitly amended.

           4. Constellation Equity
                  No platform may be disadvantaged by calibration or governance
                  decisions.

           5. Lineage Transparency
                  All temporal decisions must be recorded in lineage.

       These principles cannot be suspended.

RIGHTS
       The constitution guarantees rights to platforms, constellations, and
       operators.

       Platform Rights:
           • right to stable resonance baselines
           • right to harmonic-phase clarity
           • right to fair calibration
           • right to ancestry preservation
           • right to sync-field access

       Constellation Rights:
           • right to unified standards
           • right to cross-platform interoperability
           • right to epoch-level stability
           • right to anomaly protection

       Operator Rights:
           • right to transparent lineage
           • right to calibration auditability
           • right to override unsafe states (within constitutional limits)

DUTIES
       Duties define what RTT systems must uphold.

       Platform Duties:
           • maintain harmonic-phase stability
           • preserve sweep ancestry
           • report resonance drift
           • comply with calibration directives

       Constellation Duties:
           • maintain sync-field integrity
           • propagate standards updates
           • coordinate epoch transitions
           • enforce anomaly protocols

       Governance Duties:
           • maintain primary standards
           • ensure calibration fairness
           • preserve lineage continuity
           • protect constitutional invariants

CONSTITUTIONAL INVARIANTS
       Invariants are rules that cannot be violated under any circumstances.

       Invariant categories:

           resonance invariants
                  • R₀ must remain globally consistent
                  • resonance windows cannot be falsified

           harmonic invariants
                  • Φ₀ must be shared across platforms
                  • lock stability thresholds cannot be lowered

           temporal invariants
                  • epoch boundaries must be recorded
                  • sweep ancestry cannot be erased

           sync invariants
                  • sync-index definitions cannot be altered
                  • sync-field baselines must remain traceable

           lineage invariants
                  • lineage cannot be rewritten
                  • lineage must remain complete

AMENDMENT MECHANISMS
       Amendments allow the constitution to evolve.

       Amendment requirements:
           • 3/4 majority of all standards councils
           • approval by WRSADC
           • lineage recording of amendment
           • constellation-wide calibration event

       Amendment types:
           • baseline updates
           • epoch redefinitions
           • new invariants
           • governance restructuring

ENFORCEMENT
       Enforcement ensures constitutional compliance.

       Enforcement mechanisms:
           • calibration mandates
           • sweep-window restrictions
           • Δv correction requirements
           • sync-field realignment
           • lineage correction notices

       Enforcement escalation:
           1. advisory notice
           2. calibration directive
           3. operational restriction
           4. constellation intervention

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Lineage records:
           • constitutional amendments
           • rights and duties changes
           • invariant violations
           • governance decisions
           • epoch transitions

       Lineage ensures constitutional continuity across epochs.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • enforces constitutional invariants
           • executes governance protocols
           • maintains standards traceability
           • coordinates calibration authorities
           • blocks unconstitutional states

       WRSADC is the constitutional executor.

NOTES
       The orbital constitution is the foundational document of RTT systems.
       It ensures that resonance-time remains stable, interoperable, and
       traceable across platforms, epochs, and mission domains.

